## Future pre-build resource gate (for a later Owner execution prompt)

Minimum observation: **5 minutes**, ≥5 samples, ~60s apart.

Reject the build if **any** of:

- HTTP health ≠ 200
- collector not exactly one online target / restart loop
- idle-in-transaction > 0 or ≥60s unexpected xact
- active CREATE INDEX / REINDEX on telegram_messages
- available RAM < 4 GiB
- root free < 10 GiB
- swap-out (`so`) > 0 on a majority of samples
- **median** data-device (`dm-0`) `%util` ≥ 80 **and** median iowait ≥ 10
- **any two consecutive** samples with dm-0 `%util` ≥ 95 and iowait ≥ 10

One favorable sample must not override a bad window.

Do not reason that C2 must be built while the disk is saturated because MAX
queries cause the pressure.

